    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's the standard response they always give. But honestly, it feels like they're just using vague \"long-term\" goals to ignore the pretty immediate reality of companies going under right now. Does it seem like their arguments actually hold up when you look at the economic data, or is it mostly just moral positioning?",
